{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-torus-knot-top-channel-decoration","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:torus-knot-top-channel-decoration","kind":"definition","title":"Top-channel decoration $\\delta^{\\mathrm{top}}_q(T_{m,p}) = q^{w} - q^{-w}$ of a torus knot","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-delta-q-decoration"],"tags":["delta-q","torus-knot","writhe","bar-involution","alpha-em","pre-archimedean"],"defines":["torus-knot-top-channel-decoration"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.TorusKnotTopChannel.topChannelDecoration","text":"torus-knot-top-channel-decoration.md","leanSource":"torus-knot-top-channel-decoration.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:torus-knot-top-channel-decoration\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{m,p}</code> be a positive torus knot presented on its braid index, so that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m \\le p</code>, as the closure of the braid <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta_{m,p} = (\\sigma_1\\sigma_2\\cdots\\sigma_{m-1})^{p} \\in B_m</code>. Its writhe is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w = (m-1)p</code>. In the trivial one-dimensional representation of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_m(q)</code>, where every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i</code> acts by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>, the braid acts by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^{w}</code>. The <dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-torus-knot-top-channel-decoration\">top-channel decoration</dfn> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{m,p}</code> is the bar-odd part of this eigenvalue under the bar involution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\mapsto q^{-1}</code>:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\delta^{\\mathrm{top}}_q(T_{m,p})\n  \\;:=\\;\n  q^{w} - q^{-w},\n  \\qquad\n  w = (m-1)p.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-top-channel-decoration.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.24.9","page":"b/def-torus-knot-top-channel-decoration","lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.TorusKnotTopChannel.topChannelDecoration","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-top-channel-decoration.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
